+\subsection{Best Practices for Simulating Low-Altitude UAS Radar Signals}
+The simulation section is intentionally written as a review checklist. A radar expert should be able to confirm that the benchmark does not hide an unrealistic clean signal behind good classifier numbers. EchoForge therefore reports the carrier/bandwidth/CPI assumptions, the range and velocity resolution implied by those assumptions, the target and hard-negative cadence priors, the receiver impairments, and the non-Gaussian clutter/RFI families. The run is still synthetic, but it is not an unlabeled black box.
