+\subsection{Scenario Setup: Take-Up, Climb, and Cruise}
+Each positive scenario group expands into three phase records. The initial take-up window is deliberately noisy: the target is closest to ground coupling, launch transient artifacts, and unsettled kinematics. The climb-transition window increases separability but still stresses aspect changes and multipath. The cruise window is the cleanest of the three because track rate, aspect, and prop cadence are most stable. Hard negatives follow the same phase expansion so that the model cannot learn phase index as a label shortcut.
