+\section{Sensor Fusion: Why the Comparator Matters}
+Sensor fusion is not a decoration in this benchmark; it is the accepted-practice comparator. Single branches expose useful but incomplete evidence. X/Ku range-Doppler and micro-Doppler summaries are strong against some birds and clutter but can overreact to RC prop cadence and multipath. S-band and GBAD-style cueing broaden coverage but have coarser resolution or stale-track stress. Acoustic cues are vulnerable to weather/traffic, while passive-RF cues are sparse and can be absent for RF-silent objects. Fusion earns its role by combining these imperfect views while penalizing stale or low-provenance cues.
+
